# EnvironmentPostProcessor implementations are loaded through SpringFactoriesLoader,
# which reads this file. The META-INF/spring/<name>.imports convention is only for
# auto-configuration classes, so registering the post-processor there did nothing -
# the application started with no profile and failed later with Spring's generic
# "Failed to configure a DataSource" instead of the message that says to set ENV.
org.springframework.boot.env.EnvironmentPostProcessor=\
com.app.config.RequiredProfileEnvironmentPostProcessor
